{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1715","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Monoblock"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Stanley has decided to buy a new desktop PC made by the company \"Monoblock\", and to solve captcha on their website, he needs to solve the following task."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"awesomeness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of an array is the minimum number of blocks of consecutive identical numbers in which the array could be split. For example, the awesomeness of an array "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1, 1, 1]$$$ is $$$1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[5, 7]$$$ is $$$2$$$, as it could be split into blocks $$$[5]$$$ and $$$[7]$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9]$$$ is 3, as it could be split into blocks $$$[1]$$$, $$$[7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7]$$$, and $$$[9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$. There are $$$m$$$ queries of two integers $$$i$$$, $$$x$$$. A query $$$i$$$, $$$x$$$ means that from now on the $$$i$$$-th element of the array $$$a$$$ is equal to $$$x$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After each query print the sum of awesomeness values among all subsegments of array $$$a$$$. In other words, after each query you need to calculate $$$$$$\\sum\\limits_{l = 1}^n \\sum\\limits_{r = l}^n g(l, r),$$$$$$ where $$$g(l, r)$$$ is the awesomeness of the array $$$b = [a_l, a_{l + 1}, \\ldots, a_r]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line you are given with two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n, m \\leq 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the next $$$m$$$ lines you are given the descriptions of queries. Each line contains two integers $$$i$$$ and $$$x$$$ ($$$1 \\leq i \\leq n$$$, $$$1 \\leq x \\leq 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the answer to each query on a new line."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 5\n1 2 3 4 5\n3 2\n4 2\n3 1\n2 1\n2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n29\n23\n35\n25\n35\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After the first query $$$a$$$ is equal to $$$[1, 2, 2, 4, 5]$$$, and the answer is $$$29$$$ because we can split each of the subsegments the following way: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1; 1]$$$: $$$[1]$$$, 1 block; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1; 2]$$$: $$$[1] + [2]$$$, 2 blocks; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1; 3]$$$: $$$[1] + [2, 2]$$$, 2 blocks; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1; 4]$$$: $$$[1] + [2, 2] + [4]$$$, 3 blocks; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1; 5]$$$: $$$[1] + [2, 2] + [4] + [5]$$$, 4 blocks; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[2; 2]$$$: $$$[2]$$$, 1 block; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[2; 3]$$$: $$$[2, 2]$$$, 1 block; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[2; 4]$$$: $$$[2, 2] + [4]$$$, 2 blocks; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[2; 5]$$$: $$$[2, 2] + [4] + [5]$$$, 3 blocks; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3; 3]$$$: $$$[2]$$$, 1 block; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3; 4]$$$: $$$[2] + [4]$$$, 2 blocks; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3; 5]$$$: $$$[2] + [4] + [5]$$$, 3 blocks; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[4; 4]$$$: $$$[4]$$$, 1 block; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[4; 5]$$$: $$$[4] + [5]$$$, 2 blocks; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[5; 5]$$$: $$$[5]$$$, 1 block; "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" which is $$$1 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 1 + 2 + 1 = 29$$$ in total."}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1715C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1715/problem/C"}